/-!
# Étale cohomology of the roots of unity on an affine smooth curve

Let `X` be an affine smooth curve over an algebraically closed field `k`, let `n` be invertible
in `k`, let `X ⊂ X̄` be a smooth projective compactification, `g` the genus of `X̄` and `r` the
number of points of `X̄ ∖ X`. [Stacks, Tag 03RR] asserts

```
H⁰_ét(X, μ_n) = μ_n(k),   H¹_ét(X, μ_n) ≅ (𝐙/n𝐙)^{2g + r - 1},   H^q_ét(X, μ_n) = 0 for q ≥ 2.
```

Clause (1) is `AlgebraicGeometry.baseRootsToEtaleH0_bijective_of_isIntegral`, where it carries its
own unconditional registration of the tag. This file registers clauses (2) and (3), on the *same*
site and at the same coefficient
universe: the small étale site `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.topology` cut out of a big étale
site, with abelian coefficients `AddCommGrpCat.{u}`. That is also the site of [Stacks, Tag 03RQ]
in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityAllDegrees`, whose
apparatus — the Kummer sequence `AlgebraicGeometry.kummerSmallEtale`, the identification
`H¹_ét(X, 𝐆_m) = Pic(X)` of [Stacks, Tag 03P8] and the canonical map
`AlgebraicGeometry.etaleH1RootsOfUnityToPicard` — this reuses throughout rather than rebuilding.

## The degree-one exact sequence, and what it is not

The source's statement for the *projective* curve has `H¹_ét(X, μ_n) = Pic⁰(X)[n]`, because every
invertible global function on a proper variety over an algebraically closed field is an `n`-th
power, so the Kummer boundary out of the global units vanishes. On an *affine* curve that is
false — `Γ(𝐆_m, 𝒪)ˣ = k^* × 𝐙` — and the Kummer sequence gives instead an extension

`0 ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ/(Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ)^n ⟶ H¹_ét(X, μ_n) ⟶ Pic(X)[n] ⟶ 0`,

whose two ends are **proved here with no hypothesis beyond invertibility of `n`**:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.etaleH1RootsOfUnityToPicard_eq_zero_iff`, that a class dies in `Pic(X)`
  exactly when it is the Kummer boundary of a global unit, together with
  `AlgebraicGeometry.ker_etaleH1RootsOfUnityToPicard_eq_range_kummerBoundaryHom` identifying that
  kernel with the range of `AlgebraicGeometry.kummerBoundaryHom`, whose own kernel is the `n`-th
  powers by `AlgebraicGeometry.kummerBoundary_eq_zero_iff`;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_etaleH1RootsOfUnityToPicardNTorsion`, that the canonical map onto
  the `n`-torsion of `Pic(X)` is onto.

Both ranks in that extension depend on the compactification in a way the two summands of
`2g + r - 1` do not separate: writing `R ⊆ Pic⁰(X̄)` for the subgroup generated by the classes
`𝒪_{X̄}(x_i)` of degree zero and `s` for its rank, the units contribute `(𝐙/n𝐙)^{r - 1 - s}` and
`Pic(X)[n]` has order `n^{2g + s}`. The source avoids `s` by restricting from `X̄` instead, through
the four-term sequence
`0 → H¹_ét(X̄, μ_n) → H¹_ét(X, μ_n) → ⊕_{i=1}^r 𝐙/n𝐙 → 𝐙/n𝐙 → 0`;
either way the total is `2g + r - 1`, and either way that total is a *rank count*, which is what
`hrank` below carries.

## What is unconditional, and what is carried

Unconditional, at the source's hypotheses and nothing more:

* the two ends of the degree-one sequence above;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nsmul_sheafH_rootsOfUnitySheaf_eq_zero`, that `H^q_ét(X, μ_n)` is
  annihilated by `n` — the roots-of-unity sheaf is the kernel of `n · 𝟙` on the sheaf of units,
  so `n · 𝟙` vanishes on it and hence on its cohomology;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_addEquiv_fin_zmod_of_surjective`, that an extension of a free
  `ℤ/nℤ`-module of finite rank by another is free of the sum of the ranks. This is the step that
  turns a rank count into the source's `(𝐙/n𝐙)^{2g + r - 1}`, and it is genuinely needed: an
  extension of abelian groups `0 → (𝐙/n𝐙)^a → G → (𝐙/n𝐙)^b → 0` need not split, but one of
  `ℤ/nℤ`-*modules* does, the quotient being free hence projective, and `G` is a `ℤ/nℤ`-module
  precisely by the annihilation above;
* `AlgebraicGeometry.subsingleton_etaleH2_rootsOfUnity_of_divisible`, clause (3) in degree two
  from the `n`-divisibility of `Pic(X)`, and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.subsingleton_etaleH_rootsOfUnity_of_three_le`, clause (3) above it.

Carried as explicit named hypotheses by the statements *of this file*:

* `hGm`, the vanishing `H^q_ét(X, 𝐆_m) = 0` for `q ≥ 2`, which is [Stacks, Tag 03RM]. It is
  **proved** outright, as
  `AlgebraicGeometry.subsingleton_sheafH_kummerSmallEtale_X₂_smoothCurve`, with no hypothesis at
  all; the forms of the statements below with it supplied rather than carried are in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityAffineCurveGmVanishing`. The
  library proves Tag 03RM as
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.subsingleton_sheafH_multiplicativeSheaf_smoothCurve`, unconditionally —
  no form of [Stacks, Tag 03Q9] is carried there any more — but on *Mathlib's* small étale site
  and at a different coefficient universe. The two coefficient
  categories differ in universe, but this is not an obstruction to `hGm`: the comparison of the
  two sites blocks nothing:
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.toEtaleSite`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isDenseSubsite_toEtaleSite`,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.sheafEquiv` and
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DenseSubsiteGlobal.sheafCohomologyIsoOfIsEquivalence` are all available, and
  `sheafEquiv` is an equivalence `Sheaf (SmallEtale.topology B S hS) A ≌ Sheaf
  (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology S) A` for a *fixed* coefficient category `A`. Nor do the two `A`s
  ever agree. Elaborated, `(kummerSmallEtale B X hX n).X₂` has type
  `Sheaf.{u, u, u + 1, u + 1} (SmallEtale.topology.{u} B X hX) AddCommGrpCat.{u}`, because
  `AlgebraicGeometry.unitsPresheaf` on a `Scheme.{u}` takes values in `AddCommGrpCat.{u}`;
  whereas `Stacks.Kummer.multiplicativeSheaf.{u₁, u₂} X` has type
  `Sheaf.{u₁, max (u₁ + 1) u₂, u₁ + 1, max (u₁ + 2) (u₂ + 1)} (Scheme.smallEtaleTopology.{u₁} X)
  AddCommGrpCat.{max (u₁ + 1) u₂}`, because `Stacks.Kummer.multiplicativePresheaf` ends in
  `AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max (u + 1) v, u}` and `AlgebraicGeometry.unitsPresheaf` does not;
  since `max (u₁ + 1) u₂ ≥ u₁ + 1 > u₁`, no choice of `u₂` brings `multiplicativeSheaf` to
  `AddCommGrpCat.{u}`. **That asymmetry is exactly what makes the comparison free.** Restriction along the dense-subsite embedding is
  precomposition with a functor of sites, which commutes with the postcomposed
  `AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor` that distinguishes the two spellings; so the restriction of `𝐆_m`
  from Mathlib's site *is* the coefficient-universe lift of the middle term of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.kummerSmallEtale`, definitionally. The site comparison therefore runs at the
  upper coefficient universe `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}`, and the coefficient universe descends
  afterwards on this site alone, by
  `Stacks.Cohomology.CoefficientLift.subsingleton_cohomology_of_ulift`. The statements below keep
  `hGm` as an explicit hypothesis so that they stay available over a weaker input, exactly as
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityDegreeTwoPicard` keeps its
  `hdeg`, and the discharged forms are assembled downstream.
  On Tag 03RM's *own* site this hypothesis is not needed at all: there clause (3) of this tag is
  registered with Tag 03RM *consumed* rather than carried, on
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.subsingleton_sheafH_rootsOfUnitySheaf_two_le_of_nsmul_surjective`, which
  carries only the divisibility.
* `hdvd`, the `n`-divisibility of `Pic(X)`. For the affine curve the source gets it from the
  surjection `Pic⁰(X̄) ↠ Pic(X)`, available because `r ≥ 1`, and the divisibility of `Pic⁰(X̄)`,
  which is [Stacks, Tag 03RP] for the Picard scheme of [Stacks, Tag 0BA0]. Note the spelling:
  because `Pic(X)` *is* a quotient of `Pic⁰(X̄)` here, divisibility of all of `schemePicard X` is
  the correct hypothesis for the affine curve, where on a smooth projective curve it would be
  false — `Pic(X)` surjects onto `𝐙` — which is why
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityDegreeTwoPicard` spells its
  own `hdvd` on `AlgebraicGeometry.curvePicardDegreeZero` instead.
  Of Tag 03RP the library has *three* registrations: commutativity, on
  `AlgebraicGeometry.isCommMonObj_of_isProper_of_geometricallyIntegral`; clause (3), that `[d]` is
  onto on an abelian variety, as `Stacks.Groupoids.surjective_zpow_id_left_of_flat`; and
  clause (4), that `A(k)` is divisible over an algebraically closed field, as
  `Stacks.Groupoids.exists_zpow_eq_of_flat` — the last two over the flatness of `[d]` as their one
  hypothesis. `Stacks.Groupoids.exists_nsmul_eq_of_surjective` transports clause (4) to any
  additive group `A(k)` surjects onto, in exactly the `∃ y, x = n • y` shape `hdvd` has, so it
  would discharge `hdvd` outright. What is missing is the abelian variety, not the divisibility of
  its rational points: `AlgebraicGeometry.picardScheme` does exist, as
  `(picardFunctor …).reprX` under a representability instance ([Stacks, Tag 0B9Z]), but it carries
  no `CategoryTheory.GrpObj` and no `AlgebraicGeometry.IsAbelianVariety`, and none of Tag 0BA0's
  eleven registrations supplies either; nor is the surjection `Pic⁰(X̄) ↠ Pic(X)` in the library.
* `hunits`, `htors` and `hrank`, the rank count of the degree-one sequence. `htors` is the
  punctured analogue of the `hgenus` of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_etaleH1ConstantZModAddEquivGenusPow` and rests on the same two
  tags. `hunits` is the divisor theory of the punctures, and the honest part of it is proved, at
  greater generality than a curve:
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UnitsBoundaryValuations.units_quotient_free_finrank_lt_of_isNormal`
  and `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.UnitsBoundaryValuations.exists_linearEquiv_units_quotient` show,
  for a normal proper variety `Y` of any dimension and a nonempty open `V ⊆ Y` with `r` boundary
  points of codimension one, that `Γ(Y, V)ˣ/k^*` is free abelian of rank `m` with `m + 1 ≤ r`.
  The *inequality* is a theorem; **equality is false in general**, holding exactly when the
  differences `[x_i] - [x_j]` are torsion in `Pic⁰(X̄)` and failing already for an elliptic curve
  minus two points whose difference has infinite order (`r = 2`, the group trivial, `m = 0`). So
  only the total `2g + r - 1` is unconditional, which is why `hrank` carries the total and nothing
  here claims an exact `r - 1`. Two further steps would be needed even for the inequality to reach
  `hunits`: the identification of `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ` with `Γ(X̄, V)ˣ` along the open immersion, and the
  base change of `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ/k^* ≅ 𝐙^m` to `Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ/(Γ(X, 𝒪_X)ˣ)^n ≅ (𝐙/n𝐙)^m` using the
  divisibility of `k^*`.

## What this file registers

Clauses (2) and (3) carry the tag here, as hypothesis-carrying registrations: every hypothesis
beyond the source's is an explicit named argument, named in the attribute string, and none is an
axiom, an unproved placeholder or a weakening of the conclusion, as in the registration of all
eight clauses of [Stacks, Tag 03RQ] on
`AlgebraicGeometry.etaleCohomology_rootsOfUnity_smoothProjectiveCurve_allDegrees`.

* `AlgebraicGeometry.nonempty_etaleH1RootsOfUnityAddEquivZModPow` registers clause (2) over the
  rank count alone, carrying `hunits`, `htors` and `hrank` and neither `hGm` nor `hdvd`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.etaleCohomology_rootsOfUnity_affineSmoothCurve` registers clauses (2) and
  (3) together on this site, over all five.
* Clause (3) alone, with Tag 03RM consumed rather than carried, is registered on Tag 03RM's own
  site, as
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.subsingleton_sheafH_rootsOfUnitySheaf_two_le_of_nsmul_surjective`
  in `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityDegreeTwo`.
* Clause (1) keeps its own unconditional registration on
  `AlgebraicGeometry.baseRootsToEtaleH0_bijective_of_isIntegral`, at full integral generality.
* The forms of these statements with `hGm` supplied rather than carried are in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.Curves.RootsOfUnityAffineCurveGmVanishing`,
  together with the degrees `q ≥ 3` of clause (3) *unconditionally* and clauses (1) and (3) over
  `hdvd` alone — the two clauses in which the genus and the number of punctures do not occur.

